course: dictionary
lesson: 14698
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around the word, and ask yourself what the sentence is about.
explain: «Lily's first primer had big pictures of a cat and a red ball.» Here a primer is a first, easy book for learning to read. The pictures and the word first are the clues.
explain: «Before Dad painted the shed, he brushed on a primer so the green paint would stick.» Now primer is paint, the first coat that helps the top paint stick. Dad painted before he brushed, so the clue is the paint.
fact: A primer is a first, easy book for learning to read or to count, or a short book that teaches the basics of a subject.
fact: Primer can also mean the first coat of paint, which helps the top paint stick.
fact: A primer can be a small part that sets off a firework or a bullet.
fact: Primer is a noun, and its plural is primers.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Lily's first primer had big pictures of a cat and a red ball.» What is a primer here? | A bag for shopping | A small part of a firework | *A first, easy book for learning to read | A tin of paint
exercise: «Before Dad painted the shed, he brushed on a primer so the green paint would stick.» What does primer mean here? | A book of sums | A dog's collar | A small part that sets off a firework | *A first coat of paint that helps the top paint stick
exercise: «The tiny primer inside the firework sets off the big bang.» What is the primer? | A first coat of paint | *A small part that sets off the firework | A long story about the sky | A school reading book
test: «The old maths primer had many easy sums on every page.» What is a primer in this sentence? | A tin of paint | A cloth for wiping the desk | A small part of a firework | *A first, easy book that teaches the basics
test: «Mia painted the wood with primer first, then with bright blue paint.» Why did she use primer first? | To make the wood smell nice | To hide the wood under a cloth | *So the blue paint would stick well | To scrub the wood clean
exam: «Grandma learned to read from a primer in a school long ago.» Which meaning of primer fits? | A first coat of paint | A small part that sets off a firework | A large, heavy sack | *A first, easy book for learning to read
